      "side": 1,
      "message": "This code path is probably not going to be well tested. Instead, can the check be in maybeConfigureStaticIp, so that the common code paths are used instead ? Such as:\n\nmStaticIpv4ClientAddr \u003d maybeParseStaticIpv4ClientAddr(mStaticIpv4ServerAddr, request.staticClientAddress);\n\nprivate static Inet4Address maybeParseStaticIpv4ClientAddr(LinkAddress serverAddr, String clientAddr) {\n    // Only allow static client IP assignment if the server also has a static IP, and the client is in the right subnet\n    if (serverAddr \u003d\u003d null || TextUtils.isEmpty(clientAddr)) return null;\n    final InetAddress addr \u003d (Inet4Address) InetAddresses.parseNumericAddress(clientAddr);\n    if (!PrefixUtils.asIpPrefix(serverAddr).contains(addr)) return null;\n    return (Inet4Address) addr;\n}\n\nNote the additional check for the client address to be in the right subnet too.\nThis follows a pattern to check external inputs where they are parsed, and then not worry about consistency of the parameters.",
